Article 32

Social rehabilitation as referred to in Article 26 paragraph (1) letter number is a service provided by assistants to restore the traumatic condition of victims.

(1 Social rehabilitation as referred to in paragraph (1) is carried out by: (2)

a. providing guidance and counseling;
b. psychological recovery of victims;
c. accompanying victims in the family and community environment; and d. providing Safe Houses for victims of violence who require ongoing treatment.

Special social rehabilitation for women victims of domestic violence and trafficking in persons is carried out by: (3)a. providing guidance and counseling;
b. psychological recovery of victims;
c. accompanying victims in the family and community environment; d. providing skills training and education; and €. providing business capital assistance.

Social rehabilitation as referred to in paragraph (1) is implemented by Regional Apparatus having principal tasks and functions in the fields of: (4)

a. social affairs;
b. Cc.  d. women's empowerment and child protection; education health; ande. mental and spiritual.

In addition to being implemented by Regional Apparatus as referred to in paragraph (4), social rehabilitation may also be implemented by the community or social service (5) institutions.

CHAPTER II PREVENTION OF VIOLENCE AGAINST WOMEN AND CHILDREN Part One Forms of Violence Against Women and Children Article

Forms of violence against women and children include:

a.
c. d.  f. physical violence;

psychological violence;

sexual violence; neglect;

exploitation; and/or other violence.

Article Physical violence as referred to in Article letter constitutes an act that results in pain accompanied by injury, wounds or disability to the body, miscarriage, unconsciousness and/or causes death of women and/or children.

Article Psychological violence as referred to in Article letter constitutes an act that results in fear, loss of self-confidence, loss of ability to act, feelings of helplessness and/or psychological suffering to women and/or children. Article Sexual violence as referred to in Article letter includes:

a. acts in the form of sexual harassment;
b. coercion of unnatural or unwanted sexual relations; and/or c. coercion of sexual relations with others for commercial purposes and/or certain purposes.

CHAPTER VII

INVESTIGATION

Article 44

In addition to Investigating Officers of the State Police of the Republic of Indonesia, investigations of criminal acts as referred to in paragraph (1) of this Regional Regulation may be carried out by Civil Servants within the Bengkalis Regency Government whose appointment is determined in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations.

Civil Servant Investigators as referred to in paragraph (2) of paragraph (1) are authorized to:

a. examine the truth of reports or information concerning criminal acts related to violence against women and children;
b. examine any person and/or business entity suspected of participating in criminal acts related to violence against women and children in the business environment;
c. request information from any person and/or business entity in connection with criminal acts related to violence against women and children;
d. examine evidence materials, records, or other documents concerning criminal acts related to violence against women and children;
e. conduct examinations at certain places suspected of containing evidence materials;
f. carry out seizures of goods and materials resulting from violations that can be used as evidence in criminal cases related to violence against women and children;
g. request assistance from experts in the framework of carrying out investigative duties concerning criminal acts related to violence against women and children; and
h. terminate the investigation if there is insufficient evidence of the existence of criminal acts related to violence against women and children.

In carrying out their authority, Civil Servant Investigators as referred to in paragraph (1) shall coordinate with the Indonesian National Police in accordance with the provisions of paragraph (3) of laws and regulations.

4. Investigators as referred to in paragraph (1) shall notify the commencement of the investigation and submit the results of their investigation to the Public Prosecutor through the Investigator Officer of the Police of the Republic of Indonesia in accordance with the provisions regulated in the Criminal Procedure Code.

