c. women and children victims of violence, regulations are needed to guarantee efforts to implement the provision of protection of women and children in the Region; that based on the considerations as referred to in letter a, letter b, and letter c, it is necessary to establish a Regional Regulation concerning the Implementation of Protection of Women and Children;

CHAPTER II PREVENTION OF VIOLENCE AGAINST WOMEN AND CHILDREN Part One Forms of Violence Against Women and Children Article

Forms of violence against women and children include:

a.
c. d.  f. physical violence;

psychological violence;

sexual violence; neglect;

exploitation; and/or other violence.

Article Physical violence as referred to in Article letter constitutes an act that results in pain accompanied by injury, wounds or disability to the body, miscarriage, unconsciousness and/or causes death of women and/or children.

Article Psychological violence as referred to in Article letter constitutes an act that results in fear, loss of self-confidence, loss of ability to act, feelings of helplessness and/or psychological suffering to women and/or children. Article Sexual violence as referred to in Article letter includes:

a. acts in the form of sexual harassment;
b. coercion of unnatural or unwanted sexual relations; and/or c. coercion of sexual relations with others for commercial purposes and/or certain purposes.

Article 41, the Regional Government may partner with the business sector, NGOs/social organizations concerned with women and children in the protection of women and children from acts of violence.

Partnership as referred to in paragraph (1) is carried out through: (2)

a. notification of employment opportunity information for women victims of violence;
b. education and training for women and children victims of violence;
c. educational assistance for women and children victims of violence who have been withdrawn from their education; d. fostering and increasing the economic independence of women victims of violence;
e. providing a complete and easily accessible information system;
f. building networks and cooperation with law enforcement apparatus, government apparatus, universities, the private sector and various non-governmental organizations concerned with women and children from various forms of violence; and/org. opening complaint posts for the protection of women and children from various forms of violence up to the Village level.

Partnership as referred to in paragraph (1) and paragraph (2) is set forth in the form of an agreement in accordance with (3) the provisions of laws and regulations.

Article 23

Prevention as referred to in Article 22 letter a, is implemented by: (1)

a. establishing a network in efforts to prevent violence against women and children;
b. conducting coordination, integration, and synchronization of violence prevention based on partnership patterns;
c. establishing a system for preventing violence against women and children;
d. conducting socialization regarding laws and regulations related to the protection of women and children victims of violence;
e. providing knowledge about prevention and mechanisms for overcoming violence against women and children; and
f. enhancing the role and value of local wisdom and the role of customs in the protection of women and children.

Prevention as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be implemented in an integrated manner by Regional Apparatus that (2) have main duties and functions in the fields of:

empowerment of women and protection of children; education;

health;

social affairs and manpower;

youth and sports; and
f. mental and spiritual.

Regional Apparatus in preventing acts of (3) violence against women and children as referred to in paragraph (1) may involve related agencies.

In addition to being implemented by Regional Apparatus and related agencies as referred to in paragraph (3), prevention (4) is also implemented by:

a. family and/or closest relatives;
b. community, NGOs, universities, community organizations, social organizations and religious organizations; and
c. business world.

Procedures for preventing acts of violence against women and (5) children as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be further regulated by Regent Regulation.

